1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:08,800
B1 Amy is talking about her experience in a tie-dyeing workshop at school.

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,820
Listen and complete the notes below.

3
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:20,810
Yesterday we had a tie-dyeing workshop at school and it was amazing.

4
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:31,000
We used the traditional method of the Bai people of Dali in Yunnan province and made some wonderful things.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,010
I used a white t-shirt and now it's blue and white with fun patterns.

6
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:45,200
First I twisted parts of the t-shirt and tied them with string.

7
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:50,730
Then I put the t-shirt into a big bowl of dye.

8
00:00:50,730 --> 00:00:56,180
The dye got its beautiful blue colour from a special plant.

9
00:00:56,180 --> 00:01:05,710
After a few minutes of moving the t-shirt around in the dye I took it out and let it dry in the sun.

10
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:12,610
When it was dry I untied the t-shirt and saw the amazing patterns.

11
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:18,570
I really love my t-shirt and it's great to learn about traditional tie-dyeing.
